course: dictionary
lesson: 14985
title: A very exact copy
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A replica is a copy of something, and a very good one. Look at the words around it to find its meaning. «The museum has a replica of an old ship.» The museum has the ship in a copy form, because the real ship is too old or too precious to show.
explain: «Sam wore a replica shirt to the football match.» Sam's shirt looks just like the team's kit. Replica tells you the shirt is a copy of the real kit, not the real kit itself.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. Try "the museum has a copy of an old ship". Does it still make sense? Yes, so replica means a copy, and a very exact one.
fact: Replica is a noun. A replica, and the plural is replicas.
fact: A replica is a very exact copy of something.
fact: Replicas can copy ships, statues, buildings or shirts.
fact: In museums, replicas let people see what precious or lost objects looked like.
fact: In sport, replica shirts copy the kit that a team wears.
exercise: «The museum has a replica of an old ship.» What is a replica? | A ship that sails very fast | *A very exact copy of something | A very old real ship | A map of the sea
exercise: «Sam wore a replica shirt to the football match.» What is a replica shirt? | A shirt made of wool | An old shirt from a museum | *A copy of the team's kit | A shirt for swimming
exercise: Which word means a very exact copy? | *replica | ship | ancient | museum
test: «The park has a full-size replica of a lion.» What does replica mean here? | A small toy lion | A photo taken at the zoo | A real lion | *An exact copy of a lion
test: Why do museums show replicas? | *To let people see what a precious or lost object looked like | To sell the real objects | To make the rooms look bigger | To hide the real objects
exam: Which sentence uses replica correctly? | The replica of the castle was made of real stone | Replica is a loud noise made by a castle | *The children built a replica of the castle from wood | We went to the replica and ate lunch on the hill
